Subject: [PATCH] Present: once the swap chain has shown pictures it is kept; stuck pictures pause the hand-over (TODO 393)

The user's RX 7900 XTX froze at an alt-tab: GL's copies into Direct3D's textures stopped finishing (the GPU had hung), 5 s
later the watchdog of 0196 sent the window to GL's own swap, and the window's thread then hung inside GL's swap ("Not
Responding"). A window that has shown a flip-model swap chain's picture stays black on GL's swap anyway (0196's own
finding on the Intel laptops), so after the first shown picture none of 0196's reasons switch paths any more: the swap
chain is kept (said once), and pictures that have not moved on for 5 s set stalled(): the window draws nothing into its
pictures and hands nothing over, never waits for them (its thread keeps reading its messages), and resumes when they
move again (said). Before the first shown picture (the Intel case of 0196) nothing changes. PS2X_PRESENT_KEEP=0: the
fallback at any time, as before. Test switch PS2X_PRESENT_STALL_TEST=<from s>,<for s>: GL's copies held unfinished for
that while (a stuck hand-over after pictures were shown, then its recovery). Also said: the present's mode (at the refresh /
at once) and whether the window is in front, each time either changes.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_host_present.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_host_present.h
index 7cdd7b4..d5bc05d 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_host_present.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_host_present.h
@@ -57,6 +57,9 @@ namespace ps2_host_present
         // pictures have not moved on for 5 s (TODO 362): present() will not work here. Also writes the watchdog's line
         // (no picture shown 10 s after the start). The window's thread, each picture.
         bool broken();
+        // (TODO 393) The pictures handed over have not moved on for 5 s after the swap chain has shown some (broken() keeps
+        // the swap chain then): nothing is to be drawn into the pictures nor handed over until it is false again.
+        bool stalled();
         void close();
     }
 }
